{"op":"add","path":"/elements/exec_summary","value":{"type":"TextBlock","props":{"content":"The Enterprise plan leads all segments with 9650 in average monthly churn MRR, making it the primary area of revenue risk (Step 1). Across 36 plan-month observations, arpu emerges as the stronger predictor of churn MRR — churn_mrr correlates more strongly with ARPU (health) (r=0.829) than customer count (r=0.23). Customer count explains 5.3% of churn variance vs 68.8% for ARPU. — confirming this is not a simple headcount problem (Step 2). Together the findings point to a concentrated, value-driven churn problem in a specific plan tier.","variant":"insight"},"children":[]}}
